cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite the paper below and this software."
type: software
title: "We Have a Deal: a research toolkit for bilateral negotiation"
abstract: >-
  An open arena for automated freight-rate negotiation. Shippers and carriers negotiate
  many bilateral tables in parallel under information asymmetry, and each negotiation
  clears through stable matching. Users plug in their own agents and benchmark them
  against the nine reference architectures of the accompanying paper; everything the
  paper reports (data, figures, notebooks, scripts) is included.
